From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Play media and capture camera and microphone on AVFoundation
 of iOS 6

A minimal AVFoundation player for video and audio elements, RevMediaPlayerAVF,
that reports its tracks, ready state, size, buffered and seekable ranges,
settles a seek, describes what plays to the now playing centre, and shows
fullscreen video in the platform movie player. Element fullscreen gets its
embedder side, time-control.css is compiled in so the scrubber has a width, the
real MediaSampleAVFObjC is built, and AVFoundation is asked which types it
plays.

getUserMedia works through an AVCaptureSession backend for camera and
microphone with a MediaStream preview player, the WebKit1 user media client,
and the preferences that turn these APIs on. Absent soft-linked symbols return
nil instead of asserting, and the newer audio session, sleep disabler and
playback target calls are guarded.
